ition":{"commit_sha":"5d2eae43f80fbef12913f330c161ac6223c05ae3","position":"1795048394547444779-df0041b4-9a4e-4c58-908d-fdeb000c44bd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"3ddbf62fd19b96c58e119973c52f253fa3532a7127b6fc626419988e2940e276","event_uuid":"689f67a0-32fd-4ffd-a834-3e754980e51e","position":{"commit_sha":"5280b3318f785c336f1759948b82a8bb821d2c32","position":"1795049200710241826-689f67a0-32fd-4ffd-a834-3e754980e51e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"771a620a1a128d0ff8a3b3d1b5349ac299b13557bf524626bc6d128a44ef2695","event_uuid":"469ffcf7-224b-4302-a57a-61fec57cb007","position":{"commit_sha":"ea808a5b18be55169d7c8ccfe2f58f59f8723ca8","position":"1795051314448960425-469ffcf7-224b-4302-a57a-61fec57cb007"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"f3d7cd385c8da4ae6142a8eb6f36f47d14919ba6737a5cd3e6a91572caf2b330","event_uuid":"2fcc3488-436d-4520-a7cb-1602c524c1c8","position":{"commit_sha":"585f8f22234514d93839900740fa566328bd3aae","position":"1795051322773236803-2fcc3488-436d-4520-a7cb-1602c524c1c8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"cd47a5b4e9b170f0049b0dcef94613809a9fab485d5effa9eb75540d713c1540","event_uuid":"b8189205-56c2-43a6-90ab-f148175277be","position":{"commit_sha":"9e6354c986700808fcc6758cfba1be570578ffac","position":"1795062833922890634-b8189205-56c2-43a6-90ab-f148175277be"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Starting evidence (read from source at b4e0d01b649, not yet tested on Windows): the product-side literal is the read-freshness throttle marker in `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py` `_sync_marker_age` (`f\"/tmp/.ticket-sync-{md5[:12]}\"`), opened for read there and for write later in `ensure_fresh`. On Windows `/tmp` is drive-relative and usually absent, so the read returns age 9999 and the write fails inside the best-effort `except`, which would mean the 60-second fetch throttle never engages and every read fetches. Test-side copies of the literal: `tests/unit/test_read_freshness_git_spawns.py:99`, `tests/unit/test_read_freshness_parity.py:139`, `tests/unit/test_compact_fold_prelock.py:152`, `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py:91`, `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_fresh_ac_material.py:47`, `tests/interfaces/store/sync_contention_harness.py:46`. Design point for the fix: `tempfile.gettempdir()` honours `TMPDIR`, so two processes with different `TMPDIR` would stop sharing one throttle on POSIX; a marker under the tracker's git dir avoids that. Expose the path through one helper the tests import instead of re-deriving it.","timestamp":1794858276048080856},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause confirmed (AC1). Windows job 133527199439 (run 43932173744): 19 tests fail with `FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '\\\\tmp\\\\.ticket-sync-<md5>'`, the literal `/tmp/.ticket-sync-*` marker path from `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:198`; the other 2 compare `str(Path(\"/tmp/x\"))` with the POSIX literal (`'\\\\tmp\\\\foo'`, `'\\\\tmp\\\\barrier'`). Product consequence: on Windows `_sync_marker_age` always returned 9999 and the marker write was swallowed, so the once-per-minute read-fetch throttle never engaged.\n\nFix (commit a8d61ab8449 locally): `sync_marker_path()` joins `tempfile.gettempdir()`; marker read/write name `encoding=\"utf-8\"`; six tests use `sync_marker_path`; docs updated; `hardcoded-tmp.args` and its `@` line in test.yml deleted (all 21 lines fixed).\n\nRegression (AC3): `tests/unit/test_sync_marker_tempdir.py` redirects `tempfile.tempdir`. Against the pre-fix reads.py: 2 failed, 1 passed (the missing-marker edge case passes either way). After the fix: 3 passed. Portability: `tempfile.gettempdir()` + `os.path.join` resolve per platform.","timestamp":1795028618630366281},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed as Gerrit 3427 (`56b4f28cf50`, rebased on `9ddb035cf59`), first of a 4-change stack (3427 tmp marker, 3428 posix shell, 3429 separators, 3430 encoding). `make verify` passed at the stack top: 21414 passed / 30 skipped default tier, 226 passed / 2 skipped integration, exit 0.","timestamp":1795037720845310317},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI finding on Gerrit 3427 patch set 1 (Verified -1, run 44402939360): the bounded mutation gate's clean-test baseline failed in 3 shards (gates, reducer-processors, signing). The repo-root leak guard reported a new `.ticket-sync-<md5>` entry in each.\n\nRoot cause: scripts/mutation_gate.py runs shard tests under bwrap with `/` read-only and only the checkout and pytest basetemp writable. With /tmp read-only, `tempfile.gettempdir()` falls through its candidate list to its documented last resort, the current directory, which is the checkout. So sync_marker_path() now put the marker in the repo root. Before this change the literal /tmp write failed and was swallowed, so nothing appeared.\n\nFix (amended into this change, patch set 2): execute_shard sets TMPDIR to the writable pytest basetemp for both sandboxed children. That gives the sandbox the writable temp dir that every real host provides, and that the ~30 src/rebar modules already using tempfile rely on. Regression test: tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py::test_shard_children_get_a_writable_temp_dir fails without the line and passes with it. Portable: TMPDIR is honoured by tempfile on every platform, and the change touches only the Linux/macOS mutation harness.\n\nmake verify on the restacked series: 21416 passed, 30 skipped, 2 failed. The 2 failures were test_a_finished_gate_drive_releases_its_event_loop, from a stale worktree venv (anyio 4.14.2 against the >=4.15 floor). After make install (anyio 4.16.0) both pass when rerun alone. The integration tier was not rerun locally because the host was loaded; CI Verified covers it.","timestamp":1795048394547444779},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patch set 3 of Gerrit 3427 (commit 6dfd8c97650, same Change-Id). It acts on the 4 LLM-Review advisories from patch set 2:\n1. The survivor-diagnosis re-run (_diagnose_non_killed) also executes mutated code in the bwrap sandbox, so it now gets TMPDIR=basetemp too.\n2. test_shard_children_get_a_writable_temp_dir now drives both sandboxed children (clean run, then mutmut run) and asserts TMPDIR on both. New test_survivor_diagnosis_gets_a_writable_temp_dir covers point 1. Both fail with the TMPDIR lines removed.\n3. file_impact now lists scripts/mutation_gate.py, tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py and .joe-janitor/tools.md.\n4. .joe-janitor/tools.md no longer describes the marker as the literal /tmp path.\n\nPatch set 2's Verified -1 came from tests/unit/test_model_classes.py::test_a_finished_gate_drive_releases_its_event_loop[raised] on py3.11 and py3.12 (run 44429902115). That test is tracked as unselfish-finnicky-whooper and is not touched by this change; the same test passed on 3430 patch set 2, whose tree includes this commit. Local reproduction on anyio 4.16.0: the per-run loop was still alive right after gc.collect() in 32 of 400 drives, and all 32 were freed within 0.5 s. That supports the delayed-release explanation recorded on that ticket.","timestamp":1795051322773236803}],"created_at":1794857684450297674,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1b8c6498-b539-44b3-9034-51c5c3fd6663","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6798-606d-37dc-46e7"},{"link_uuid":"7214bc6a-d9fb-49b5-b27f-7f4efe59a43f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f645-a3f5-edef-4dc6"},{"link_uuid":"689f67a0-32fd-4ffd-a834-3e754980e51e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5a41-8f8e-c4c7-4515"},{"link_uuid":"b8189205-56c2-43a6-90ab-f148175277be","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5c27-6c38-eb72-4989"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from majestic-depilatory-beetle. The advisory `sweep (windows)` job deselects the 21 tests in `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/hardcoded-tmp.args` (runs at `b4e0d01b649`, 2026-11-15/16). Windows has no `/tmp`, so a literal `/tmp/...` path is the drive-relative `\\tmp\\...` there.\n\nRoot cause, confirmed from Windows job 133527199439 (run 43932173744):\n\n- **Product defect.** `ensure_fresh` keeps its once-per-minute read-fetch throttle marker at the literal `f\"/tmp/.ticket-sync-{md5}\"` (`src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:198`, written at `reads.py:256`). On Windows that directory does not exist, so the marker read always fails (age 9999) and the write is swallowed: every read fetches, i.e. the throttle is off. 19 tests fail with `FileNotFoundError: ... '\\\\tmp\\\\.ticket-sync-<md5>'` because they stamp or read the same literal path (`tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_fresh_ac_material.py:47`, `tests/unit/test_read_freshness_git_spawns.py:99`, `tests/unit/test_read_freshness_parity.py:139`).\n- **Test-only.** `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_sync_logger.py:171` and `tests/unit/test_child_hooks.py:55` compare `str(Path(\"/tmp/x\"))` against the POSIX literal; Windows renders `\\tmp\\x`.\n\n## Approach\n\nKeep the marker in the platform temp directory, which is where the stdlib already puts per-host scratch: add `sync_marker_path(tracker_abs: str) -> str` in `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py` returning `os.path.join(tempfile.gettempdir(), f\".ticket-sync-{md5[:12]}\")`, used by `_sync_marker_age`. One function owns the path, so tests import it instead of rebuilding the literal. Also pass `encoding=\"utf-8\"` on the marker read/write (`reads.py:200`, `reads.py:256`). No config key, env var or flag is added.\n\nEvery test that builds the marker literal switches to `sync_marker_path`: the three above plus `tests/unit/test_compact_fold_prelock.py:152`, `tests/interfaces/store/sync_contention_harness.py:46` and `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py:91` (on macOS `gettempdir()` is not `/tmp`, so these would silently stop clearing the real marker). The two test-only asserts compare against `str(Path(\"/tmp/x\"))`. `docs/concurrency.md:943` and `docs/bash-migration.md:309` name the old path and are updated.\n\nPortability: `tempfile.gettempdir()` and `os.path.join` resolve per platform; nothing POSIX-only is introduced.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_read_freshness_git_spawns.py`, `tests/unit/test_read_freshness_parity.py`, `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_fresh_ac_material.py`, `tests/unit/test_compact_fold_prelock.py`, `tests/interfaces/store/sync_contention_harness.py`, `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py`, `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_sync_logger.py`, `tests/unit/test_child_hooks.py`\n- new regression test `tests/unit/test_sync_marker_tempdir.py`\n- `docs/concurrency.md`, `docs/bash-migration.md`\n- `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/hardcoded-tmp.args` and its `@` line in `.github/workflows/test.yml` (both deleted once every line is fixed)\n\n## Testing\n\n- Regression (Linux gate, fails before the fix): with `tempfile.tempdir` monkeypatched to a `tmp_path` subdirectory, `sync_marker_path` lands inside it, and an `ensure_fresh` call inside the window spawns no git because the marker it wrote there is read back as fresh. Edge path: a missing marker still reports age 9999.\n- The 21 listed tests pass under `make verify`.\n- Windows: `gh workflow run test.yml --ref main` after merge; the `sweep (windows)` job runs the 21 tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The class's root cause is recorded on this ticket with the evidence that confirmed it.\n- [ ] `git grep -n '/tmp/.ticket-sync' -- src tests` prints nothing on the merged tree.\n- [ ] The new regression test fails on the pre-fix `reads.py` and passes after (both outcomes recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] Every line removed from `hardcoded-tmp.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `sweep (windows)` concludes `success` on that run.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py","reason":"marker in tempfile.gettempdir via sync_marker_path"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_sync_marker_tempdir.py","reason":"new Linux-gate regression test"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_read_freshness_git_spawns.py","reason":"use sync_marker_path"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_read_freshness_parity.py","reason":"use sync_marker_path"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_fresh_ac_material.py","reason":"use sync_marker_path"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_compact_fold_prelock.py","reason":"use sync_marker_path"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/sync_contention_harness.py","reason":"use sync_marker_path"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py","reason":"use sync_marker_path"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_sync_logger.py","reason":"platform path compare"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_child_hooks.py","reason":"platform path compare"},{"path":"docs/concurrency.md","reason":"marker location"},{"path":"docs/bash-migration.md","reason":"marker location"},{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/hardcoded-tmp.args","reason":"remove fixed tests (delete when empty)"},{"path":".github/workflows/test.yml","reason":"drop @ reference once argfile deleted"},{"path":"scripts/mutation_gate.py","reason":"CI finding on PS1: sandboxed shard children get TMPDIR=basetemp so tempfile.gettempdir() does not fall back to the checkout"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py","reason":"regression tests for the sandbox TMPDIR"},{"path":".joe-janitor/tools.md","reason":"maintainer note named the old literal /tmp marker path"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","5a41-8f8e-c4c7-4515"],["relates_to","5c27-6c38-eb72-4989"],["relates_to","f645-a3f5-edef-4dc6"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"007a0506-4721-40c1-82b2-04118579dd0d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"c1cf-bf46-01a9-4b17","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: literal /tmp paths (21 tests)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["729966d1-7f3a-412c-a902-e272de9add54","8d7d6876-da68-4d11-99cf-ffc093f2d4f2","f8786e10-a349-44ed-aa25-bae3bda86f15","007a0506-4721-40c1-82b2-04118579dd0d","4207d262-f3e8-41fa-bb57-cc897bfc9a2b","3863427e-e37c-40d5-910a-6c4d14c8b41e","d1372d93-64cd-4b95-ac99-4a5a1dd88c57","7214bc6a-d9fb-49b5-b27f-7f4efe59a43f","df0041b4-9a4e-4c58-908d-fdeb000c44bd","689f67a0-32fd-4ffd-a834-3e754980e51e","469ffcf7-224b-4302-a57a-61fec57cb007","2fcc3488-436d-4520-a7cb-1602c524c1c8","b8189205-56c2-43a6-90ab-f148175277be"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795062833922890635,"uuid":"b2f82f27-9f95-40e1-a8f5-d9c060e942e3"}